<title>ITALY: Italy's Milan sees May CPI at 0.2 pct mo/mo.</title>
<headline>Italy's Milan sees May CPI at 0.2 pct mo/mo.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Milan said its May consumer price index stood at 0.2 percent month-on-month and 1.6 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>In April Milan's inflation rate was 0.3 percent and 1.8 percent respectively.</p>
<p>Milan is one of 11 Italian cities to have published CPI data on Tuesday and Wednesday. The city's CPI has a weighting of 19.1 percent on the national index. The 11 sample cities have a combined weighting of 75.66 percent on the total index.  </p>
<p>Following is the breakdown of the price changes.</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to April 1997):</p>
<p>					    Month/Month     Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		     0.2     (0.3)   1.6   (1.8)</p>
<p>    Food				  0.2    (-0.2)  -1.1   (0.0)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	   0.0     (0.4)   2.7   (2.9)</p>
<p>    Housing and utility charges   0.0     (1.1)   5.2   (5.1)</p>
<p>    Furniture			   0.2     (0.0)   1.4   (2.0)</p>
<p>    Health services		   0.2     (0.1)   3.5   (3.4)</p>
<p>    Transportation		    0.4     (0.0)   0.5   (0.1)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture    -0.4     (0.4)   0.1   (0.5)</p>
<p>    Education			   0.0     (0.0)   3.9   (3.9)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants	  0.1     (0.5)   2.7   (2.8)</p>
<p>    Other goods or services	 1.6     (0.1)   2.8   (1.4)</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129526</p>
</text>
